    title: "Spot checks, inventory reconciliation and expected deliveries (staff)",
    body: `Daily spot check: every weekday the app picks one item at each location (never the same item twice until every item has had its turn, then it starts over). The warehouse manager counts it from the Home card (or [Inventory](/inventory) > Spot check): type what's on the shelf (spray foam lot by lot) and "Save count". The app's number isn't shown, so it's a real count. If it matches, it's approved automatically (its LAST COUNTED date and COUNTED BY go onto the spreadsheet). If not, it goes to an admin to approve before stock changes. A weekday that isn't counted stays on the list with a red alert until it's done.
Inventory reconciliation (the quarterly count): [Inventory](/inventory) > "Perform Inventory Reconciliation" > Start. Every item (spray foam by lot) is listed by category; type each count, it saves as you go (stop and come back any time), "Not counted yet" shows what's left, and a blank item isn't changed. Then "Send for approval". An admin opens it (Home > Waiting on you, or [Counts](/inventory/counts)), checks the differences ("App had", "Counted", "Difference") and taps Approve or "Don't approve". A number counted wrong (a display item missed, digits swapped)? The admin taps "Edit count" next to the item, types the right number (and why) and Save: the first number counted is kept and shown, and if the count then matches the app it's approved automatically. A reconciliation where everything matched is approved automatically too.
Variance report: [Counts](/inventory/counts) > "Variance report" (or [Reports](/inventory/reports) > "Variances (print)") lists every item whose last count didn't match the app and hasn't been approved (waiting, or not approved), by location, with the difference, its value and what the app has now. "Print / save PDF" prints it. Approved differences go onto the spreadsheet: TOTAL IN STOCK on the COUNT SHEET, or Adj on FOAM LOTS for spray foam, with who counted it. Anything picked up after the count is already taken into account.
Expected deliveries: [Receiving](/inventory/incoming) > "Expected delivery": who it's from, the day it's expected, PO # / BOL # (optional) and the items and quantities. It shows on the warehouse calendar. When the truck arrives, open it: it's a Receiving Report with the expected lines filled in. Snap the BOL if you like (the app fills in what it says), enter what actually came (spray foam needs the lot #, and the Mfg and Exp dates if you have them) and tap "Receive: add to stock". Everything else is added to TOTAL IN STOCK; spray foam goes onto FOAM LOTS (a new lot gets its own row, a lot already there gets Shipped In).`,
